# DECISIONS.log — append-only ADRs

## ADR-0001 … ADR-0009
See earlier entries: PixiJS renderer, fixed 60Hz sim, JSON content, door mats,
gesture-gated audio, pure engine modules, renderer-owned ambience, A* grid
pathfinding, seekers sharing the pathfinder.

## ADR-0010: Mini-game rules as pure cores, DOM as a replaceable host — 2026-08-08
Context: prototype mixed game rules with DOM code, making them untestable.
Decision: all 9 mini-games have pure logic cores in `minigames/logic.ts`
(mastermind scoring, haggle state machine, etc.); `runtime.ts` is a thin DOM
host that could be swapped for a Pixi-native UI later.
Consequences: every game is unit-tested in node; UI reskinning never touches
rules.

## ADR-0011: Interiors are a separate top-down scene, not iso — 2026-08-08
Context: rooms in the prototype used a simple top-down grid while the city is
isometric. Decision: keep interiors top-down (8×5) with their own runtime and
renderer; the world switches modes (city | interior) rather than faking
interiors inside the iso map.
Consequences: simpler furniture collision, clearer readability, and the two
renderers never fight over the camera.
